<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9093"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 8:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The definite victims, and any others that are now known.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9093-->
<!--Post: 9228--><!--Time: 1109438856-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9228"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marine Hedge, your murderer has been brought to justice.  may you rest in peace.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9228-->
<!--Post: 9288--><!--Time: 1109463507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neverstop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neverstop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 4:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> Now that this suspect is identified it would be very helpful to know from you what you had observed over the years if anything, about D.R. Or about his family members. Please don&#39;t feel you have to identify names. But all of us who are concerned about this phenomenon of sadistic stranger-murder, which is increasing as our societal controls continue to crumble, want to know what might possibly give these characters away. Could he have tipped anyone off by his behavior? Could a non-family member have spotted &#34;something amiss&#34;? If you don&#39;t want to venture into this question you might consider responding by first creating a new username. Thanks, we need your input.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9288-->
<!--Post: 9879--><!--Time: 1109684484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9879"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 5:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Neverstop, I just returned last night from my folks in Park City. My sister and I spent Sunday hanging No Trespass signs to ward off the reporters. It is crazy! We are all sickend and in shock. We always knew that Marine was murdered by BTK, we just would have never dreamed that we knew her killer or that he lived so close! I will tell you that Dennis never picked on my folks, and they have the largest lot in the area! I&#39;m thinking the reason - maybe because my folks and one other neighbor lived in that area long before he ever did. And, my mother bitched him out about 5 years ago for not picking up a tree limb out of the middle of the street! HA! She was Irish! I still wonder why he didn&#39;t retaliate on her. Nevertheless, when I have had the opportunity to gather my thoughts, I&#39;ll post my observations!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9879-->
<!--Post: 9893--><!--Time: 1109694982-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with one profiler - he started leaving the bodies for the public to find because he lived too close and didn&#39;t want anyone to know who he is. It does make sense! He started doing this with Marine! But, how did he get from 21st &amp; Woodlawn after he dumped her car there? That is the question that plaques us all!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9893-->
<!--Post: 9955--><!--Time: 1109712893-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9955"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 1:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, I still don&#39;t think he did all this alone, call me crazy, but I agree with Charlie O. someone helped him. Or mailed his letters, or picked him up after the crimes. Just can&#39;t put my finger on it right now, But when we started looking at the other Victims two weeks ago, that is when things started making sense, LE was concentrating on the one&#39;s they were sure of and not the ones in Park City. That was their first mistake, letting Rader control, weither or not he told them who he killed<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9955-->
<!--Post: 10150--><!--Time: 1109786256-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10150"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember: see my post under theories! Again, there were some of my family members questioned for 2 hours after Marine was found. I believe it was because they worked at Coleman! This was 1985! Almost 10 years after Denny the dog catcher worked there. I don&#39;t know why they didn&#39;t suspect him then, possibly because he only worked there a year.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10150-->
<!--Post: 10152--><!--Time: 1109786561-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok - Let me add to that. I know that the investigation was focused on Marine&#39;s employment and boyfriend at the time. Don&#39;t ask me to elaborate. Yes, the WPD did screwup with their focus being in that direction, and I&#39;m certain it was because Denny the dog catcher&#39;s MO changed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10152-->
<!--Post: 10261--><!--Time: 1109860351-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 6:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He modified his MO but his signature was the same. Since LE looks at the living area of the victims for a possible perp, they would have been looking in Rader&#39;s neighborhood. He was merely avoiding detection, like a good SK. Anger, control, bondage, strangulation, posing, mementos: the tools of his trade and his trademark. Just because there was no semen at these other crime scenes, does not mean that it was not BTK. He could get off later on the excitation of the murder. Fire setting, just like posing the victim, is another way to know that the crime is still ongoing after the killer has left the scene. Killers mature as they refine their methods and careers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10261-->
<!--Post: 10356--><!--Time: 1109908114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 7:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To all of the above - how did DTDC get from 21st and Woodlawn back to his home? Did he have some help - dare I say his brothers?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10356-->
<!--Post: 10364--><!--Time: 1109915431-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, This really isn&#39;t too complicated. I could do it myself without anyone ever knowing. <BR> He could have seen her at the restaurant and followed her home in his vehicle, parked his vehicle near her house, took a bicycle from his vehicle and pedeled a block or two to her house and went in and killed her. Then put her body and his bicycle in her car and drives her car with her body and his bicycle in it and disposes of the body and tosses the purse. He now drives to the parking lot where he parks her car, takes his bicycle out and pedels back up to near her house where his vehicle has been parked. Puts the bike back into his vehicle and drives home. <BR>Nobody see his vehicle parked in front of her house because it&#39;s a block or two away. Nobody sees him hitchiking from where her car was dumped because he&#39;s on a bike. He&#39;s not there very long. As long as it takes to park a car unload a bike get on it and pedel away. Nobody sees him dump the body because nobody is around. He dosen&#39;t need to call anybody to come get him because he&#39;s taken a bicycle with him to get back to where he&#39;s parked his vehicle.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10364-->
<!--Post: 10378--><!--Time: 1109917755-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10378"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno - This would be a very long bike ride from 21st and Woodlawn to Independence. Someone needs to map that! Although it is certainly possible.  Wouldn&#39;t his church be a halfway point? Isn&#39;t it on Hillside and 53rd?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10378-->
<!--Post: 10393--><!--Time: 1109919637-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10393"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 11:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, since I&#39;m not from Wichita and have only passed through it once it&#39;s hard for me to have a minds eye of the area and all these known and possible BTK events but on the maps it looks like it might be a five mile bike ride from where her car was found to back to her house. That&#39;s an easy ride in the early morning with fewer cars on the roads. <BR>He would have been 40 years old at the time and we know it wouldn&#39;t have been that physically strenuous for him. Temperatures would have likely been in the 50&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10393-->
<!--Post: 10474--><!--Time: 1109968802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linda Shaw was murdered four months after Marine, we know Rader was out killing during this time sorry for the strange post, trying to link the timeline to possible vics.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10474-->
<!--Post: 10590--><!--Time: 1110040176-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10590"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 8:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno - your right! Now I&#39;m racking my brain trying to remember if I ever saw his bike. You know now that I give it some more thought - he might have utilized the park behind their houses to hide that bike. Does anyone remember seeing a bike in the pic with the big storage shed? &#40;Not the small one attached to his house&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10590-->
<!--Post: 10591--><!--Time: 1110040309-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10591"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 8:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E - is Ms. Shaw listed as a cold case somewhere?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10591-->
<!--Post: 10603--><!--Time: 1110055485-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10603"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky-  Ember is talking about Linda Shawn Casey<!--/Text--></td></tr>
