<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10679"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks V - I figured that out!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10679-->
<!--Post: 10680--><!--Time: 1110132493-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10680"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 10:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno: I asked my family about that bike ride and they said it was certainly possible. However, none of them remember a bike around his house.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10680-->
<!--Post: 10737--><!--Time: 1110170960-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok look at him, does he look like he ever rode a bike<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10737-->
<!--Post: 11090--><!--Time: 1110422818-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11090"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was there some boy scout activity that would have required him to?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11090-->
<!--Post: 11206--><!--Time: 1110502923-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11206"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 5:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage, I agree that the 2005 Dennis Rader isn&#39;t a contender for the Tour d&#39;France but this was 20 years ago. <BR>Rocky, If he did use a bike to accomadate the commission of a crime he wouldn&#39;t have taken the chance of it being his own I don&#39;t think. He would have stole one that was left unattended for a one time use, took it with him and then dumped it before he got home.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11206-->
<!--Post: 11220--><!--Time: 1110507331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11220"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, <BR> <BR>I meant to acknowledge your bicycle post a few days ago. <BR> <BR>It is a brilliant solution. Great thinking as usual J. <BR> <BR>Raider chose occupations that helped facilitate his criminal activity. <BR>Naturally, his recreation and exercise regimen would be conducive to getting away with murder as well. <BR> <BR>Circa 1985 <BR> <BR>I can picture him in touring gear, on a prized 12-speed road bike, roaming the flat blacktop stretches of Park City and beyond -- waving to pedestrians and police, making mental notes, rehearsing and becoming invisible. <BR> <BR>He had a bike rack on his vehicle, or more likely, he drove a van. <BR>He regularly loads up the bike, driving out to the country for a long ride. <BR> <BR>There goes Dennis again! <BR> <BR>an alibi <BR>a confounding method <BR>an escape <BR>and a cardio-vascular workout <BR>on two wheels <BR> <BR>LD <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11220-->
<!--Post: 11227--><!--Time: 1110511031-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 7:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;He was one of those people who, when you went camping, you could always depend on to have brought all the equipment you needed.&#34;  <BR>- George Martin Co-Leader &#40;along with Dennis Rader&#41; Boy Scout Troop 491. Quoted March 2005.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11227-->
<!--Post: 11338--><!--Time: 1110592073-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11338"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 5:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, I&#39;ve read and seen that quote on T.V. But, why did he do this to Marine on his wife&#39;s birthday? That just sickens me that he would do it on his wife&#39;s birthday. Maybe his wife didn&#39;t like Marine for some reason &#40;I could never ever imagine why&#41; and he did it for her!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11338-->
<!--Post: 11380--><!--Time: 1110646110-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11380"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 8:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You know Rocky, it&#39;s interesting you say that.  The thought has actually crossed my mind several times that perhaps the motive for all these murders was that Rader was taking out people that wronged his wife/family - defending the family honor so to speak.  As the victims suffered he would tell them who he was and how it was so wrong to cross his wife or kids and now they would die for that transgression.  Perhaps the Otero&#39;s were a personal revenge for him and he found a sick sense of satisfaction in it. Later ones could have been either for himself or his wife.  Murders committed even later were exacting revenge for anyone in the family - himself, his wife, and his kids - perhaps even his parents, in-laws, or siblings. <BR> <BR>I really don&#39;t want to believe this is so because it would mean someone in his family should have been able to connect the dots &#40;boy, evertime I tell hubby/dad about this person who dissed me they end up dead.....&#41; but stranger things have happened in this world.   <BR> <BR>Ironically it was reading about the supposed blogs posted by Kerri Rader&#39;s husband telling of her waking screaming in the night that got me thinking about this.  Maybe she wasn&#39;t the victim of abuse, but knew something &#40;on a conscious or unconscious level&#41; about her father killing people.  I personally never saw any of the blogs, so I&#39;m not sure exactly what was and was not stated.  <BR> <BR>Had Kerri Rader looked into her father&#39;s secret shed when she was younger?  Did she perhaps see him enter Ms. Hedge&#39;s home on the day she went missing?  As a child growing up there are innumerable opportunities to observe your parents as they really are, not how they present themselves to the public.  Additionally, a child by nature is inquisitive and very observant and may notice odd little things that most adults miss.  And finally most kids tend to be curious about &#39;forbidden&#39; areas and snoop around when given an opportunity &#40;although my experience finds this trend tends to run much stronger with boys as opposed to girls&#41;. <BR> <BR>Also working against this theory is all the information that is coming out about Rader - the control, the bullying &#40;of some&#41;, the ego/power trip, etc.  This information does seem to paint a picture of someone capable of committing these monstrous acts without needing &#39;motivation&#39; from others.  Yet, he also seems like the type who would overreact to the little &#39;disses&#39; that are occasionally thrown our way.  Some of the information we know about him infers that he was courteous and respectful to the women he worked with and dealt with at church &#40;not allowing dirty jokes to be told around them, helping with errands, etc.&#41; - maybe he had real issues with anybody who he felt wronged his wife or daughter.  &#40;And obviously he had two very different personas because it seems he had no apparent problems with torturing and murdering women and children&#41;. <BR> <BR>Anyway, I&#39;ve rambled long enough.  However, Rocky I&#39;m really glad you wrote what you did because that thought had crossed my mind as well and it allowed me to share this motive theory with the group.  Thoughts, anyone??? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11380-->
<!--Post: 11397--><!--Time: 1110668269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11397"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 2:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I had been wondering myself about the birthday, that is a terrible thing, then it brought up something Johno made me aware of. Seems like everytime there was a stressor in his life, A birth, a family get together, being out of work, Rader was able to keep it together in from of his family, yet inside knew he wasn&#39;t in control of the situation, He took it out on others. Just speculation at this time, I am truly sorry Rocky that it happened at all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11397-->
<!--Post: 11407--><!--Time: 1110675646-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11407"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 5:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marine Hedge was taken from her home between 1 and 7am. Do we know much about the details of this murder i.e. what she was wearing when found, or if there was evidence that she had gone to bed that night? If she was taken during the night, could it be that DR&#39;s wife was out of town because it was her birthday? Did she go away to visit relatives for her birthday? If not, did he leave home on the pretext of &#39;checking on a malfunctioning alarm&#39; {he worked for the alarm company back then}. &#34;Honey I have to leave for awhile...back asap&#34;. <BR>If Marine was taken after DR left for work {say 6am} he would be taking a mighty big risk to do that in the morning, so close to his home.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11407-->
<!--Post: 11409--><!--Time: 1110675999-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11409"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 5:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Go up to the top of the thread and read what VErm wrote about the case, it will tell you when Marine was taken. And that is a good point about how he got out of the house. Have to find an answer for that Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11409-->
<!--Post: 11417--><!--Time: 1110686833-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11417"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 8:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember, I have similar thoughts on what was going on in his life at the times of murders. I feel like its more about when dennis wasnt the main attraction, the star, the center of attention... <BR>during wifes pregnancy, birthdays, im sure he felt crappy about himself when he was out of work in 91. I also think that as his kids got older, and he finished up the job of raising a family, he came back out to play, to finish his game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11417-->
<!--Post: 11425--><!--Time: 1110693191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11425"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 9:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lc, now that I&#39;ve given it more thought it just wouldn&#39;t be him and his wife but his inlaws too! They live around the corner. I don&#39;t recall hearing of any squables between the two families, but I know some of Marine&#39;s kids would have been about the same age of Paul&#40;Dietz&#41;Rader. That&#39;s very interesting, thanks for the insight!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11425-->
<!--Post: 11450--><!--Time: 1110754146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11450"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 2:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OMG Rocky go to the symbol thread asap and read what I  was sent about Paul it fits<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11450-->
